.TH ONRECORD 1 "2026-11-27" "onrecord 0.1.0" "Retrospective Line"
.SH NAME
onrecord \- append-only self-verifying claim store for agent memory
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B onrecord add
.I record.jsonl
.B \-\-text
.I TEXT
.B \-\-asserter
.I NAME
.B \-\-at
.I ISO8601
.B \-\-evidence
.I SRC:REF
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B onrecord
.BR get | subject | due | check
.I record.jsonl
.RI [ arg ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B onrecord
maintains an append-only JSONL ledger of attributed, timestamped,
evidence-backed claims keyed by position-bound Canonical Form 1 IDs
.RB ( claim-<16hex> ).
Updates append superseding claims without overwriting history, and supersession forks are refused (coordinate concurrent
.B add
writers externally until cross-platform file locking in PR #49 lands).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.BI "add " "record.jsonl " "[required and optional flags]"
Validate, derive position-bound ID, and append one claim line (optional
.BR \-\-supersedes ,
.BR \-\-subject ,
.BR \-\-due ).
.TP
.BI "get " "record.jsonl claim_id"
Return one claim and its full supersession chain as JSON.
.TP
.BI "subject " "record.jsonl subject_name"
Return the live head claim and chain, or a conflict object.
.TP
.BI "due " "record.jsonl YYYY-MM-DD"
List live claims whose due date is on or before the given date.
.TP
.BI "check " "record.jsonl"
Recompute every claim ID and verify linear chain soundness from line 0.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Command succeeded and record is sound.
.TP
.B 1
Validation defect, unknown ID/subject, supersession fork, or I/O refusal.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line usage error.
.TP
.B 120
Standard output or standard error stream flush failure.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
onrecord check examples/demo_record.jsonl
onrecord subject examples/demo_record.jsonl deploy
onrecord due examples/demo_record.jsonl 2026-06-01
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/david-engelmann/onrecord
